pplicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRANO KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUMITOMO SPEC METALS</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UEDA MASAMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRANO, KENJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUMITOMO SPECIAL METALS CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UEDA, MASAMI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRANO KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UEDA MASAMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRANO, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UEDA, MASAMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A first embodiment of the inventive maraging steel which has an essential composition: C: 0.01 % or less, Ni: 8 to 19 %, Co: 8 to 20 %, Mo: 2 to 9 %, Ti: 0.1 to 2 %, Al: 0.15 % or less, N: 0.003 % or less, O: 0.0015 % or less, balance: Fe, and has the component segregation ratios for Ti and Mo in its structure of 1.3 or less each; and another embodiment of the inventive maraging steel which has the above composition and contains a non-metal substance having a size of 30  mu m or less. The second embodiment of maraging steal can be easily prepared by subjecting to appropriate plastic working a steel ingot having a taper Tp = (D1 - D2) x 100/H of 5.0 to 25.0 %, a height-diameter ratio Rh = H/D of 1.0 to 3.0, and a flatness ratio B = W1/W2 of 1.5 or less.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte dans une première exécution sur un acier maraging essentiellement composé de: C: 0,01 % ou moins; Ni: 8 à 19 %, Co: 8 % à 20 %, Mo: 2 à 9 %, Ti: 0,1 à 2 %, Al: 0,15 % ou moins, N: 0,003 % ou moins, O: 0,0015 % ou moins, et d'un reliquat de Fe, et présentant un taux de ségrégation des composants pour le Ti et le Mo de sa structure, de 1,3 ou moins pour chacun d'eux, et porte dans une deuxième exécution sur un acier maraging de même composition comportant en outre une substance non métallique d'une granulométrie de 30  mu m ou moins. Cette deuxième variante se prépare facilement en faisant subir à un lingot d'acier une déformation plastique appropriée selon: une décroissance Tp = (D1-D2) x 100/H, de 5 à 25 %, un rapport hauteur/diamètre Rh = H/D, de 1,0 à 3,0, et un rapport d'aplatissement B = W1/W2, de 1,5 ou moins.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>